ve a weak upper body and I knew that  this wasn't going to be fun  I think that that slope that first slope  really hit me in my glutes and I felt  like I wasn't going to make it but I  kept a consistent pace and having the  music is really helpful to get through  it at some point I had to stop and walk  a little but then I instead of getting  defeated I remembered how when I did  marathon training that even like a short  rest gives you so much more energy and  then I was able to like take off and  finish the run I'm actually very shocked  that I did that in that amount of time  because I usually run like a 10-minute  mile I think I was just terrified of  failing and that first hill was so steep  and I was never the same again but that  being said this was actually my fastest  mile pace I've run in years  so I passed I feel good about it I'm  slightly surprised I really thought I  was gonna fail on that mile and a half  run so I'm glad that I didn't I'm kind  of proud of myself I think I did pretty  well  FBI fitness test wasn't as challenging  as I thought it was gonna be it does  make me a little sad that I was able to  crush the FBI test and makes me wonder  if they shouldn't have a little a little  higher benchmark now that I passed this  I kind of feel unstoppable I feel like I  should be in a James Bond movie or  something to celebrate  I'm gonna have some ice cream and I'm  gonna go work out in the morning feeling  pretty good about myself
 

